Arara Code: first launch opens in the system language using the built-in language packs.

Why a patch: the main process picks the UI language before any extension runs,
reading languagepacks.json, which the shared process only writes after the first
window opens. Without the file, the first launch (and the setup) was English even
with pt/es packs built in. When the file is missing, read the built-in packs'
manifests with the same shape and hash the shared process writes later.
Touches: src/vs/base/node/nls.ts

